The only difference I can see is the loss of some attributes when switching to CSV. The number of columns is the same. If you return a keyval from the reducer (mine doesn't and you didn't share yours), keys will be added as additional columns in CSV but not in native, where they remain separate in a key value frame. To make the two more comparable you could just wrap the result with a data.frame call. But the result is more columns, not fewer.

