Now all of the values are in $val for output. This seems like an acceptable tradeoff. If I just return the full aggregate.data.frame result and don't end the reduce function with a keyval call, I get 7 columns in the csv output case for out$val but I get only 5 columns when I don't specify an output format.

A little quirky I guess but livable.

