From u6ac7e7dfbe4f6c38 at groups.google.com  Thu Feb 28 04:56:15 2013
From: u6ac7e7dfbe4f6c38 at groups.google.com (Antonio Piccolboni)
Date: Thu, 28 Feb 2013 04:56:15 +0000
Subject: Re: [RHadoop:#595] keyval with constant value
Message-ID: <hpla9X01eCE.-VDsflALCUwJ@rhadoop.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rhadoop/c/hpla9X01eCE/m/-VDsflALCUwJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

try
map = function(k,v) {x = rep(1, length(v)); keyval(x,x)}

R is vectorized and rmr follows that style by combination of choice and necessity. It is documented and illustrated in many examples. Using Java as a reference point will cause you lots of frustration.

Antonio

